(6061892, 889608, 17507, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PugPop:</b></div><hr/><i> I really don''t think this reflects the sprite of the challenge, everyone has two eyes.  As a portrait, try getting about 10 or 12 feet from the subject and go with a f/8 (or so) setting.  That would get most of the facial features in focus.  Very important; focus on the eyes.  That will make or break your portrait.  Also use unsharp mask to sharpen the result. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Just wondering how this comment could fail to be considered helpful.</td>', 'Originally posted by PugPop: I really don''t think this reflects the sprite of the challenge, everyone has two eyes.  As a portrait, try getting about 10 or 12 feet from the subject and go with a f/8 (or so) setting.  That would get most of the facial features in focus.  Very important; focus on the eyes.  That will make or break your portrait.  Also use unsharp mask to sharpen the result.   Just wondering how this comment could fail to be considered helpful.', '2010-06-18 14:43:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(6061896, 889866, 30214, '<td valign="top">Prash, it is a nice image, but it would be much stronger (and score would definitely reflect that) if the two bulbs were tack sharp<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-06-18 13:48:19.</i></td>', 'Prash, it is a nice image, but it would be much stronger (and score would definitely reflect that) if the two bulbs were tack sharp', '2010-06-18 14:47:31.000000', '2010-06-18 14:48:19.000000', 0),
(6061928, 889566, 24846, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, a beautiful double take!</td>', 'Congratulations, a beautiful double take!', '2010-06-18 15:33:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(6062199, 889423, 69325, '<td valign="top">obviously this is technically well done. I am, however, struggling to understand the context. is there supposed to be a correlation between the pencils the drops and the picture of the woman? or is the shot just there for its own sake?</td>', 'obviously this is technically well done. I am, however, struggling to understand the context. is there supposed to be a correlation between the pencils the drops and the picture of the woman? or is the shot just there for its own sake?', '2010-06-18 20:40:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(6062445, 889423, 105457, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smardaz:</b></div><hr/><i> obviously this is technically well done. I am, however, struggling to understand the context. is there supposed to be a correlation between the pencils the drops and the picture of the woman? or is the shot just there for its own sake? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Jason!<br/> <br/>You make a good point, and of course I can''t tell you that it''s a masterpiece ;-)<br/> <br/>The goal in making the photo was getting two water drops simultaneously in the picture, hence the double take. Since two drops were lacking a bit of interest, I started thinking of background. I could have gone with a smiley face, a flower, a lot of things.<br/>The choice for the woman was to make some eye connection with the viewer.<br/> <br/>I used two black pencils because they were easier to work with, regarding drops.<br/>The idea to turn upside down the image was so I could give the impression that the drops were bubbles ascending, thus the title.<br/> <br/>So it was just a matter of getting the elements together, without having too much of a back story of intention other than the visual one.<br/> <br/>Cheers,<br/>Joao<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-06-19 04:52:52.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by smardaz: obviously this is technically well done. I am, however, struggling to understand the context. is there supposed to be a correlation between the pencils the drops and the picture of the woman? or is the shot just there for its own sake?   Hi Jason! You make a good point, and of course I can''t tell you that it''s a masterpiece ;-) The goal in making the photo was getting two water drops simultaneously in the picture, hence the double take. Since two drops were lacking a bit of interest, I started thinking of background. I could have gone with a smiley face, a flower, a lot of things.The choice for the woman was to make some eye connection with the viewer. I used two black pencils because they were easier to work with, regarding drops.The idea to turn upside down the image was so I could give the impression that the drops were bubbles ascending, thus the title. So it was just a matter of getting the elements together, without having too much of a back story of intention other than the visual one. Cheers,Joao', '2010-06-19 05:52:26.000000', '2010-06-19 05:52:52.000000', 0),
(6062454, 889423, 55956, '<td valign="top">wow Joao, fantastic capture. very well done. comgrats for the ribbon :)</td>', 'wow Joao, fantastic capture. very well done. comgrats for the ribbon :)', '2010-06-19 06:28:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6062485, 889836, 62357, '<td valign="top">My money was definitely on this being yours :)  I love it.  I don''t know if my vote would have nudged you over the 5.00 or not, but I am very disappointed to see this score so low.</td>', 'My money was definitely on this being yours :)  I love it.  I don''t know if my vote would have nudged you over the 5.00 or not, but I am very disappointed to see this score so low.', '2010-06-19 08:58:51.000000', NULL, 0),
