(6461469, 889874, 113142, '<td valign="top">Not quite the brown! Though this one does deserve it, that special place for images that are amazing but others don''t understand, fear it, and give it an abyssmal score. mad props. I do, however, agree on your assessment of using the color image, far more striking. NYC brings out the weirdo in all of us . . .</td>', 'Not quite the brown! Though this one does deserve it, that special place for images that are amazing but others don''t understand, fear it, and give it an abyssmal score. mad props. I do, however, agree on your assessment of using the color image, far more striking. NYC brings out the weirdo in all of us . . .', '2011-07-05 00:37:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(6729543, 889874, 143086, '<td valign="top">this is an awesome image</td>', 'this is an awesome image', '2012-04-02 11:23:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(6933514, 889418, 5112, '<td valign="top">Bleeding heart look almost scary here.  Interesting.  I find particularly interesting how the stem goes off into the distance, at a diagonal, almost as if the hearts are contemplating some evil deed.  The leaves are saying, "No, no, don''t go, don''t do that!"  Sorry, I tend to anthropomorphize.  And the plants tend to pythomorphize, really :)  I got to think about this picture.  I like it, but I also don''t in a curious way.  I think I am going by stereotypes as plants, in particular flowers, being "nice", and here, they feel rather aggressive to me.  Very interesting.</td>', 'Bleeding heart look almost scary here.  Interesting.  I find particularly interesting how the stem goes off into the distance, at a diagonal, almost as if the hearts are contemplating some evil deed.  The leaves are saying, "No, no, don''t go, don''t do that!"  Sorry, I tend to anthropomorphize.  And the plants tend to pythomorphize, really :)  I got to think about this picture.  I like it, but I also don''t in a curious way.  I think I am going by stereotypes as plants, in particular flowers, being "nice", and here, they feel rather aggressive to me.  Very interesting.', '2012-12-15 13:07:17.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
